desc:Devil [Arcana synth] (GFX)
//tags: instrument synth drone formant vowel organ ring-modulator phaser delay reverb dark industrial arcana
//author: GardenFX
// by JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument, gfx-voice and gfx-clip (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// THE DEVIL (card XV of the GFX Arcana series): bondage to the material, the pull of temptation, heat and shadow.
// A multi-tier drone and quad-voice formant synth: two drones that burn on by themselves (a SUB DRONE and a MID DRONE
// with a pitch-WAVER), four MIDI-played voices (two organs, two synths) through a vocal tract you steer on an XY pad,
// and an industrial chain (PHASER, the ADP MOD ring modulator, a TAPE DELAY, a dark cavernous REVERB). The drones run,
// MIDI plays the voices.
//   SUB DRONE  a detuned pair of band-limited saws, a square an octave down (SUB -1) and a saw an octave up (OCT +1),
//              each with its level (OSC, SUB -1, OCT +1); DETUNE (0 - 50 cents between the pair); TONE (a 12 dB
//              low-pass, 55 Hz - 10 kHz); its own LFO: RATE (0.02 - 10 Hz), SHAPE (Sine, Triangle, Random: a smooth
//              wander), DEPTH, and LFO TO: PITCH (+/- 50 cents), LEVEL (a slow swell) or TONE (+/- 2 octaves); DRIVE
//              (the house drive: +30 dB into the anti-aliased knee clipper, the drive-tracking pre-filter and knee,
//              level-matched); LEVEL; and its sends to the PHASER, RING, DELAY and REVERB.
//              PLAY (lit) starts the drones (they swell in over about a second and die away when it is off); it loads
//              off and presets never start it. TRANSPORT (lit by default): REAPER's play / record presses PLAY and its
//              stop releases it; PLAY still works by hand. Off, PLAY ignores the transport. ROOT
//              (C .. B) and OCTAVE (0 - 3: A in octave 1 is A1, 55 Hz) set the sub's note; FOLLOW (lit): the lowest key
//              held sets the root's pitch class instead (kept when the keys are let go). The root glides (150 ms).
//   MID DRONE  the same voice, an octave above the root plus INTERVAL (unison .. two octaves, every chromatic step):
//              OSC, SUB -1, OCT +1, DETUNE (the pair split left / right), TONE, its own LFO, DRIVE, LEVEL, sends.
//   WAVER      the mid drone's pitch sweeps: SHAPE (Centre-Up-Centre: up and back; Centre-Down-Centre; Up / Down: a
//              slow trill above and below; Sine; Triangle), RATE (0.01 - 8 Hz) or SYNC (lit) to the song's grid
//              (1/8 .. 16 bars, locked to REAPER while it plays, free at the project tempo while stopped), DEPTH (0 -
//              12 semitones: how far it sweeps from the centre, either way for the bipolar shapes). The mod wheel can deepen it (WHEEL).
//   VOICES     four monophonic voices: ORGAN I, ORGAN II (nine tonewheel drawbars, band-limited, with a key CLICK;
//              REGISTRATION: Full, Flutes, Gospel, Reed, Hollow, Bright), SYNTH I (a band-limited saw) and SYNTH II (a
//              band-limited pulse, PULSE W). MODE (lit keys): ROTATE (each note to the next voice in turn), LAST NOTE
//              (up to four notes; a fifth takes the oldest; when a key is let go its voice returns to a key still held
//              that is not sounding), LAYER (one note plays all four, legato while a key is held, back to the last
//              key still held). SPREAD detunes the four against each other (cents), GLIDE (0 - 1 s), VELOCITY.
//              Each voice: four formants in CASCADE (a vocal tract: F1 - F4 as resonant peaks over the throughput),
//              then a 12 dB low-pass (CUTOFF, key-tracked by half; ENV: the FILTER envelope's depth, +/- 6 octaves),
//              then its own DRIVE (the house drive). The AMP / FILTER keys pick which envelope the four knobs (ATTACK,
//              DECAY, SUSTAIN, RELEASE) set. LEVEL and the four sends. Pitch bend (BEND: 0 - 12 semitones), sustain.
//   VOICE MORPH the XY pad (drag the point; SHIFT = fine; double-click = the centre): X is the VOWEL - U, O, AW, A, UH,
//              ER, E, I, a smooth morph between neighbours (the throaty AW / UH / ER sit in the middle); Y is the
//              voices' weight: the organs at the bottom, the synths at the top (equal power; in ROTATE and LAST NOTE
//              neither family falls below 35 %, so every note still sounds; in LAYER it is a full crossfade). XY LFO:
//              Off, Orbit, Figure-8, Random walk, its RATE (0.01 - 4 Hz) and SIZE (the mod wheel can widen it).
//              FORMANTS: RESO (narrower, taller peaks), THROAT (all formants shifted -12 .. +12 semitones: a deeper or a
//              smaller tract), AMOUNT (the plain voice .. the full tract).
//   PHASER     six all-passes a side (the right side 90 degrees on), RATE, DEPTH (the sweep from 160 Hz up 1 - 6.5
//              octaves), FEEDBACK, MIX (its return is the all-pass chain: it notches against the dry sound). IN.
//   ADP MOD    the ring modulator: CARRIER (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw: band-limited), FREQ (1 - 3000 Hz), DRIVE (the
//              ring's product into the anti-aliased soft clipper, level-matched), MIX. IN.
//   TAPE DELAY SYNC (lit) to a division (1/16 .. 1 bar) or TIME (20 ms - 2 s); FEEDBACK (through TONE, a 60 Hz
//              high-pass and the tape's soft limit), TONE, WOW (a slow swing, a little flutter and a wander), MIX. IN.
//              The phaser's and the ring's returns feed it a little.
//   REVERB     eight long lines (Hadamard), four diffusers, a 22 ms pre-delay: SIZE (and with it the decay, 1.5 - 17 s),
//              DARK (the damping, 6.5 kHz down to 650 Hz), MIX. IN. The delay's echoes and the other returns feed it.
//   FATE       the series' drift (0 - 100 %, 50 % = the standard amount), all three of the Devil's at once:
//              TEMPTATION (the mid drone slowly pulls away from its interval and back, up to about half a semitone,
//              and its waver deepens / settles and quickens / slows), POSSESSION (the XY point wanders on its own:
//              slow changes of vowel and of the organ / synth weight), FURNACE (the drives and the sub's heat - its
//              level and tone - build and cool over minutes). The voices also drift a little in pitch.
//   VOLUME, LEVEL, SAT (the output soft clip is always on).
// The display: the sub against the mid as a Lissajous (their phase interference), the waver's path (the last 7.5 s),
// the XY point's path, and FATE's three drifts. MIDI: notes, pitch bend, mod wheel (WHEEL: waver depth or XY LFO
// size), sustain (CC64), all notes off (CC120 / 123); channel select. MIDI passes through.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc
import gfx-clip.jsfx-inc

